Derived from makeip but NOT in this directory
---------------------------------------------

Three functions elsewhere in mkdcdisc do the same job as a makeip counterpart,
and are noted here so that this directory is not read as the complete list. They
were written against mkdcdisc's own types rather than copied, carry none of
upstream's expression, and stay MIT where they are:

    update_ipbin_crc()      src/ip_boot.cpp     cf. update_crc(), crc.c
    is_valid_peripherals()  src/ip_boot.cpp     cf. _check_peripherals(), field.c
    detect_image_format()   src/mr_image.cpp    cf. detect_file_type(), utils.c

update_ipbin_crc() is the clearest of the three: upstream reaches into a 32K
buffer at hard-coded offsets 0x40 and 0x20, while mkdcdisc addresses named
fields of its own IPBin struct and asserts that the two the checksum spans are
adjacent. What it shares with upstream is the layout of a Dreamcast boot header,
which is a fact about the hardware.

See README.md for what these files expose and how they are reached.
